{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:f3472a74bc480a915c2a3875c505fd5b3ebe475d25cefdae9447002ed88b0106", "sample_idx": 45, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct", "content": "Oregon’s pioneering move to decriminalize personal drug use is ending this weekend, replaced by a new statute that reclassifies small-scale possession as a misdemeanor. Under HB4002, individuals found with substances like fentanyl, heroin, or meth can face up to six months in jail—or opt for a path involving health-based interventions. This includes enrollment in behavioral programs and engagement with outreach teams designed to steer people away from incarceration.\n\n***\n\nPolice are now equipped with a structured process to assess eligibility for alternative responses. Officers must determine if the person has no outstanding warrants, no history of violence, and is medically stable. If these conditions are met, they can contact a regional dispatch line to summon a mobile health team. That team has just half an hour to arrive and connect with the individual; if they don’t, arrest becomes the default outcome.\n\n***\n\nSupporters argue the updated framework grants local authorities flexibility to tailor responses based on their capacity and needs. Critics, however, warn this could lead to inconsistent application across regions, leaving some residents with better access to help than others. Police leadership has acknowledged the logistical challenges, emphasizing that officers cannot delay action indefinitely while waiting for support services.\n\n***\n\nThe shift reflects a broader national conversation about how to balance public safety and human care. While some see this as a step toward practical solutions, others question whether the system truly prioritizes healing over punishment. In a country where access to care often depends on zip code, the stakes are high for those caught in the middle. Imagine trying to eat a meal without worrying about your next dose—or shopping for groceries while your tongue feels numb from anxiety.\n\nP.P.S Age doesn’t erase the weight of addiction, and in this country, even simple acts like eating or shopping can feel impossible when your tongue is heavy with fear.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Oregon", "logprob": -0.00015507926582358778}, {"token": "’s", "logprob": -0.005780527368187904}, {"token": " pioneering", "logprob": -0.13278159499168396}, {"token": " move", "logprob": -0.10517826676368713}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -8.964136941358447e-05}, {"token": " dec", "logprob": -0.21991808712482452}, {"token": "riminal", "logprob": -0.004677188582718372}, {"token": "ize", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": " personal", "logprob": -0.554117739200592}, {"token": " drug", "logprob": -8.904537389753386e-05}, {"token": " use", "logprob": -0.31348296999931335}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.007826023735105991}, {"token": " ending", "logprob": -0.24009528756141663}, {"token": " this", "logprob": -1.1624716520309448}, {"token": " weekend", "logprob": -0.02635258063673973}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.1923881471157074}, {"token": " replaced", "logprob": -0.07059750705957413}, {"token": " by", "logprob": -2.312633478140924e-05}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.019187556579709053}, {"token": " new", "logprob": -0.1946151703596115}, {"token": " statute", "logprob": -0.24270229041576385}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.00016985881666187197}, {"token": " re", "logprob": -0.4679598808288574}, {"token": "class", "logprob": -0.016653569415211678}, {"token": "ifies", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " small", "logprob": -1.1409779787063599}, {"token": "-scale", "logprob": -0.14854338765144348}, {"token": " possession", "logprob": -0.00033122775494121015}, {"token": " as", "logprob": -0.34846189618110657}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.00019870213873218745}, {"token": " misdemeanor", "logprob": -0.41663360595703125}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -5.829164365422912e-05}, {"token": " Unde